## =============================================================================
## The high-level view. Matt, 2026-09-08: "What it does page needs a much higher
## level view, not just individual feature component parts." Before this, a
## reader arriving at Features met 39 components and no account of the whole.
## =============================================================================

feat:FiveMoves
    rdf:type            ktype:Concept ;
    rdf:type            skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label          "What Reckons.AI does, in five moves" ;
    hnav:order          50 ;
    skos:broader        guide:WhatIsReckonsAI ;
    skos:definition     "Reckons.AI does one thing in five moves: it takes what you put in, works out the claims inside it, asks you which are true, keeps the ones you accept with their sources attached, and then lets you ask the result questions. Everything below is a part of one of those five moves. If you only read one thing about the product, read this page rather than the component list underneath it — the components make sense as answers to the five moves and make very little sense on their own." ;
    kpred:render-as     "gallery" ;
    kpred:page-section  "Learn" ;
    kpred:page-slug     "what-it-does" ;
    kpred:audience      "Anyone deciding whether this is the right tool, before reading about any individual capability." ;
    kpred:diagram       """flowchart LR
  IN["1 · Take it in<br/>notes, pages, feeds,<br/>things you said"]
  EX["2 · Work out the claims<br/>a model proposes<br/>facts, never writes them"]
  RV{"3 · You settle it<br/>confirm, refine,<br/>reject"}
  KP[("4 · Keep it<br/>with its sources<br/>and its history")]
  US["5 · Ask it things<br/>reckon, compare,<br/>publish"]
  IN --> EX --> RV
  RV -->|"accepted"| KP
  RV -->|"rejected"| X["Dropped, and<br/>remembered as rejected"]
  KP --> US
  US -.->|"a new question<br/>needs new sources"| IN""" ;
    kpred:diagram-caption "The five moves. Step 3 is the one that makes the rest worth anything, and it is the one no amount of automation removes." ;
    kpred:principle     "Nothing enters your graph because a model suggested it. Extraction PROPOSES; you dispose. That single rule is what separates this from a tool that reads your files and answers confidently — it is why the graph can be trusted a year later, and why it can tell you what it does not know instead of inventing an answer." ;
    kpred:constraint    "The parts below are the detail, not the argument. A component list answers what exists; it does not answer what the thing is FOR, and a reader who meets thirty-nine capabilities before meeting the loop will reasonably conclude this is a notes application with unusual settings." .

## =============================================================================
## THE FIVE MOVES, AS SETS (F187). Matt, 2026-09-09: the five moves and the six
## steps in Getting Started are great simplifications for human review.
## Each move is a skos:Collection over features that ALREADY EXIST as entities —
## the set adds the meaning, not the content. A feature may belong to more than
## one; membership overlaps rather than partitions.
## =============================================================================

set:MoveCapture rdf:type          skos:Collection ;
    kpred:set-kind      kset:page ;
    skos:prefLabel      "Take it in" ;
    skos:definition     "Paste text, point at a URL or a repository, drop in a PDF, subscribe a current to a feed so it keeps arriving, or just talk — speech to text runs locally. Extraction reads the first 12,000 characters of a source, about 2,000 words, and a longer source is cut there without a warning today; splitting long sources into chunks is planned, not built." ;
    skos:member         feat:Ingest, feat:Currents, feat:WhisperSTT, feat:TextChunking, feat:ConfluenceMigration ;
    kpred:set-relates-to feat:FiveMoves .

set:MoveExtract rdf:type          skos:Collection ;
    kpred:set-kind      kset:page ;
    skos:prefLabel      "Work out the claims" ;
    skos:definition     "A language model reads the source and PROPOSES triples, each carrying the verbatim sentence it came from. You choose the model, including a local one, and the setting that keeps everything local is a switch rather than a rewrite." ;
    skos:member         feat:LLMBackends, feat:PassageGrounding, feat:PreferLocal, feat:EntityNormalization ;
    kpred:set-relates-to feat:FiveMoves .

set:MoveSettle rdf:type          skos:Collection ;
    kpred:set-kind      kset:page ;
    skos:prefLabel      "You settle it" ;
    skos:definition     "The review queue shows what CHANGED rather than everything found: new claims, claims that contradict something you already accepted, and near-duplicates that are probably the same thing under two names. The contradictions are the valuable part — that is the moment a pile of documents would have stayed quiet." ;
    skos:member         feat:ReviewSystem, feat:ReviewWorkbench, feat:Disambiguation, feat:TrustSystem ;
    kpred:set-relates-to feat:FiveMoves .

set:MoveKeep rdf:type          skos:Collection ;
    kpred:set-kind      kset:page ;
    skos:prefLabel      "Keep it" ;
    skos:definition     "Accepted facts carry their source, the excerpt they came from, and when you accepted them. You can scrub the graph backwards through time, export the whole thing as a plain-text .ttl file, and keep several independent graphs that do not see each other." ;
    skos:member         feat:HistoryMode, feat:TTLExport, feat:MultiKB, feat:KBIdentity ;
    kpred:set-relates-to feat:FiveMoves .

set:MoveUse rdf:type          skos:Collection ;
    kpred:set-kind      kset:page ;
    skos:prefLabel      "Ask it things" ;
    skos:definition     "Describe a situation and a goal and get a proposal grounded in your own facts. Compare two graphs and see exactly where they disagree. Compress a large graph into the part that answers one question. Publish a graph as a website — these pages are that feature, running on the graph that describes this product." ;
    skos:member         feat:Reckoning, feat:Compare, feat:ContextCompression, feat:Shelly, feat:PublishedDocs, feat:LLMBackends, feat:PreferLocal ;
    kpred:set-relates-to feat:FiveMoves .

set:TheLoop rdf:type        skos:OrderedCollection ;
    kpred:set-kind      kset:story ;
    skos:prefLabel      "The loop, in five moves" ;
    skos:definition     "The whole product as a sequence. Each move is a set of its own, and the order is the point — this is a story rather than a roster, because shuffling it would describe a different product." ;
    skos:member         set:MoveCapture, set:MoveExtract, set:MoveSettle, set:MoveKeep, set:MoveUse .

<urn:reckons:set/TheLoop/member/MoveCapture>
    kpred:in-set        set:TheLoop ;
    kpred:member-entity set:MoveCapture ;
    kpred:member-order  "1" .

<urn:reckons:set/TheLoop/member/MoveExtract>
    kpred:in-set        set:TheLoop ;
    kpred:member-entity set:MoveExtract ;
    kpred:member-order  "2" .

<urn:reckons:set/TheLoop/member/MoveSettle>
    kpred:in-set        set:TheLoop ;
    kpred:member-entity set:MoveSettle ;
    kpred:member-order  "3" .

<urn:reckons:set/TheLoop/member/MoveKeep>
    kpred:in-set        set:TheLoop ;
    kpred:member-entity set:MoveKeep ;
    kpred:member-order  "4" .

<urn:reckons:set/TheLoop/member/MoveUse>
    kpred:in-set        set:TheLoop ;
    kpred:member-entity set:MoveUse ;
    kpred:member-order  "5" .

## =============================================================================
## START HERE — the page a first-time reader actually lands on.
##
## It replaces composed output: content/learn/start-here.md was an alphabetical
## dump of every section heading in the corpus, under the promise "the only page
## a new reader needs". Matt, 2026-09-06: "start here is a long list."
##
## This is an ORIENTATION page, deliberately not a duplicate of Getting Started.
## It answers the four questions a newcomer has, in the order they have them,
## and sends them somewhere real for each. The set is the sequence; the page is
## the entity — a set contributes the route, it does not define the page.
## =============================================================================

feat:StartHere
    rdf:type            ktype:Concept ;
    rdf:type            skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label          "Start here" ;
    hnav:order          1 ;
    kpred:page-section  "Learn" ;
    kpred:page-slug     "start-here" ;
    skos:definition     "Reckons.AI turns things you read into facts you have checked, and then lets you ask those facts what to do. It is not a note-taking app: the difference is that nothing is in your graph unless you accepted it, and every fact can show you the sentence it came from. Four pages below, in the order the questions usually arrive — what it is, what it does, how to start, and what it is for." ;
    kpred:audience      "Someone who has just arrived and does not yet know whether this is for them." ;
    kpred:principle     "READ THESE FOUR IN ORDER AND STOP. The rest of this site is reference, and reference read early is the reason a good tool looks complicated. If you only have five minutes, read what it does — the five moves are the whole product." ;
    kpred:constraint    "THIS TAKES LONGER TO GET VALUE FROM THAN A NOTES APP, and that is the trade rather than a rough edge. You review what a model proposes before it becomes yours, which costs you time at the start and is exactly why the answers are worth something later. If you want something that reads your files and answers confidently without asking, this is the wrong tool and that is a fine conclusion to reach on this page." .

set:FirstHour rdf:type      skos:OrderedCollection ;
    kpred:set-kind      kset:story ;
    skos:prefLabel      "Your first four pages" ;
    skos:definition     "In the order the questions usually arrive." ;
    skos:member         guide:WhatIsReckonsAI, feat:FiveMoves, guide:GettingStarted, feat:Reckoning ;
    kpred:set-relates-to feat:StartHere .

<urn:reckons:set/FirstHour/member/WhatIsReckonsAI>
    kpred:in-set        set:FirstHour ;
    kpred:member-entity guide:WhatIsReckonsAI ;
    kpred:member-order  "1" .

<urn:reckons:set/FirstHour/member/FiveMoves>
    kpred:in-set        set:FirstHour ;
    kpred:member-entity feat:FiveMoves ;
    kpred:member-order  "2" .

<urn:reckons:set/FirstHour/member/GettingStarted>
    kpred:in-set        set:FirstHour ;
    kpred:member-entity guide:GettingStarted ;
    kpred:member-order  "3" .

<urn:reckons:set/FirstHour/member/Reckoning>
    kpred:in-set        set:FirstHour ;
    kpred:member-entity feat:Reckoning ;
    kpred:member-order  "4" .

